1
00:00:07,960 --> 00:00:09,960
And who's this? He's very good.

2
00:00:11,970 --> 00:00:14,890
Oh, he's just our old gardener.

3
00:00:16,300 --> 00:00:19,420
Well, he pours better than he dresses.

4
00:00:26,742 --> 00:00:28,482
Enjoy your dinner, ma'am.

5
00:00:41,232 --> 00:00:42,232
Gardener.

6
00:01:00,770 --> 00:01:06,090
Dad. Dad, come here.
Halbrook. I got into Halbrook.

7
00:01:07,688 --> 00:01:10,988
Read it to me. My hands are dirty.

8
00:01:11,598 --> 00:01:15,658
We are pleased to offer you
a place in the class of 2021.

9
00:01:16,088 --> 00:01:18,368
Pleased. They're pleased.

10
00:01:21,758 --> 00:01:25,948
$41,000. A year. That's just tuition, Dad.

11
00:01:25,998 --> 00:01:27,018
Okay.

12
00:01:29,698 --> 00:01:32,858
Okay? That's more than you make.

13
00:01:34,107 --> 00:01:36,747
I said, okay, put the kettle on.

14
00:01:37,485 --> 00:01:40,518
I'll defer. I'll work a couple of years.

15
00:01:40,568 --> 00:01:41,848
You'll go.

16
00:01:45,118 --> 00:01:48,048
With what? You've got $11 in a coffee can.

17
00:01:48,098 --> 00:01:49,098
I've seen it.

18
00:01:49,478 --> 00:01:51,018
Then I'll find more.

19
00:01:56,128 --> 00:02:00,378
Dr. Castell, a nurse at
St. Mary's gave me your number.

20
00:02:00,428 --> 00:02:02,728
She said you pay for a kidney.

21
00:02:04,988 --> 00:02:08,588
Fifty-three. I don't drink,
I'm healthy as a horse.

22
00:02:15,037 --> 00:02:17,697
Forty. Yes, I can do Tuesday.

23
00:02:23,377 --> 00:02:25,737
You understand there's no taking it back.

24
00:02:26,695 --> 00:02:29,675
I've got two. She's got one shot.

25
00:02:32,543 --> 00:02:35,423
Most men who sit in that
chair are paying off a debt.

26
00:02:36,193 --> 00:02:40,313
I am. It's just not the
kind you're thinking of.

27
00:02:41,833 --> 00:02:45,553
Sign there. And Mr. Moore, we never met.

28
00:02:47,253 --> 00:02:48,593
Never met who?

29
00:03:10,463 --> 00:03:14,983
The Greenfield Foundation.
I've never even heard of them.

30
00:03:15,383 --> 00:03:18,603
Tuition, books, everything. Who does that?

31
00:03:19,412 --> 00:03:21,832
Rich people who feel guilty, probably.

32
00:03:28,680 --> 00:03:32,160
I'm going to find them.
I'm going to pay back every cent.

33
00:03:33,530 --> 00:03:37,330
Just go be good at it.
That's how you pay people back.

34
00:03:39,170 --> 00:03:42,360
Everybody there is going to have
parents who are judges and surgeons.

35
00:03:42,410 --> 00:03:44,710
And you'll have a dad who grows tomatoes.

36
00:03:46,190 --> 00:03:50,670
Listen to me. Dirt on your
hands is not dirt on your name.

37
00:03:51,470 --> 00:03:52,268
Hold your head up.

38
00:03:52,318 --> 00:03:56,238
Dirt on your hands, okay.

39
00:03:57,897 --> 00:03:59,757
Is not dirt on your name.

40
00:04:02,105 --> 00:04:04,145
Is not dirt on your name.

41
00:04:29,273 --> 00:04:32,833
Is that guy waving at you? Oh my god,
he wrapped them in newspaper.

42
00:04:36,322 --> 00:04:37,702
He's a friend of the family.

43
00:04:37,992 --> 00:04:40,052
Congratulations, Miss Moore.

44
00:04:41,462 --> 00:04:42,502
Ma'am.

45
00:04:57,631 --> 00:04:58,731
Did you eat?

46
00:04:59,901 --> 00:05:01,281
I'll grab something.

47
00:05:03,311 --> 00:05:04,771
That means no.

48
00:05:05,581 --> 00:05:10,281
Peanut butter. No banana,
the bananas are terrible this week.

49
00:05:11,031 --> 00:05:12,951
You don't have to keep doing this.

50
00:05:13,219 --> 00:05:17,299
Somebody does.
You'll faint in front of a judge.

51
00:05:32,178 --> 00:05:34,248
Sign where the yellow flags are.

52
00:05:34,298 --> 00:05:36,718
Whitmore trust, quarterly stuff.

53
00:05:39,168 --> 00:05:41,028
That's a lot of quarterly stuff.

54
00:05:42,866 --> 00:05:46,906
Welcome to rich people. They move
money around the way we move furniture.

55
00:05:48,024 --> 00:05:53,084
Sunday. Lunch at my sister's.
You're not backing out on me.

56
00:05:54,883 --> 00:05:56,821
I'm terrified of your sister.

57
00:05:56,871 --> 00:05:59,451
Good. That means you've met her.

58
00:06:15,609 --> 00:06:17,089
Don't touch that.
Do you know what's in there?

59
00:06:18,609 --> 00:06:20,949
Sorry, sorry. I only clean around.

60
00:06:21,188 --> 00:06:23,373
Kyle. Her name is Mrs. Alvarez.

61
00:06:23,423 --> 00:06:26,041
She's been here longer than you have.

62
00:06:26,091 --> 00:06:30,068
She's emptied your trash
every night for two years.

63
00:06:30,728 --> 00:06:32,248
Say thank you.

64
00:06:32,788 --> 00:06:33,788
Thank you.

65
00:06:37,758 --> 00:06:39,958
You didn't have to do that, Miss Moore.

66
00:06:41,876 --> 00:06:46,156
My dad always says nobody notices the people
who keep things clean until they stop.

67
00:06:46,746 --> 00:06:50,426
Your father sounds like a smart man.

68
00:06:50,704 --> 00:06:51,704
He is.

69
00:07:11,109 --> 00:07:12,869
Is that a peanut butter sandwich?

70
00:07:13,369 --> 00:07:14,171
You're a lawyer.

71
00:07:14,221 --> 00:07:15,621
Lawyers eat.

72
00:07:16,658 --> 00:07:20,138
Lawyers expense lunch. Who packed it?

73
00:07:20,218 --> 00:07:21,438
My dad.

74
00:07:22,144 --> 00:07:23,944
He cut the crusts off.

75
00:07:24,209 --> 00:07:25,849
He thinks I'm nine.

76
00:07:25,956 --> 00:07:28,596
I'm Julian. I design buildings.

77
00:07:30,776 --> 00:07:31,546
Not this one.

78
00:07:31,596 --> 00:07:34,936
Hannah! I argue in this one.

79
00:07:35,086 --> 00:07:37,686
Then let me buy you a lunch nobody packed.

80
00:07:38,846 --> 00:07:39,864
Dinner, technically.

81
00:07:39,914 --> 00:07:41,814
You don't even know my last name.

82
00:07:42,179 --> 00:07:43,859
That's what dinner's for.

83
00:07:56,654 --> 00:07:59,101
Julian says you grew up in the city.

84
00:07:59,151 --> 00:08:00,214
Which part?

85
00:08:03,363 --> 00:08:06,103
East side. Near the river.

86
00:08:06,571 --> 00:08:09,151
Oh. Near the river.

87
00:08:11,571 --> 00:08:12,571
And your parents?

88
00:08:16,539 --> 00:08:18,679
My mom died when I was nine.

89
00:08:19,488 --> 00:08:22,508
I'm sorry. And your father?

90
00:08:24,488 --> 00:08:28,528
He's retired. He travels a lot.

91
00:08:30,996 --> 00:08:32,556
What's his handicap?

92
00:08:35,491 --> 00:08:36,651
I'm sorry?

93
00:08:37,529 --> 00:08:41,089
She means golf, Mom.
Not everybody plays golf.

94
00:08:41,238 --> 00:08:45,698
She never lets me meet him.
I'm starting to think he doesn't exist.

95
00:08:47,196 --> 00:08:49,156
Or he's met your mother.

96
00:08:50,696 --> 00:08:54,636
Walter. There's a fingerprint on this.

97
00:08:56,883 --> 00:08:57,883
Apologies, madam.

98
00:08:59,133 --> 00:09:01,265
She asked me what my
father's handicap was.

99
00:09:01,315 --> 00:09:02,833
I nearly said bad knees.

100
00:09:02,883 --> 00:09:06,589
It went great. She only checked
one glass for fingerprints.

101
00:09:06,639 --> 00:09:07,703
That's love.

102
00:09:08,113 --> 00:09:10,455
I had a whole plan. A violinist, a boat.

103
00:09:10,505 --> 00:09:14,753
I'm doing it in my parents' driveway
because I can't wait anymore.

104
00:09:15,873 --> 00:09:18,713
Julian, get up, you're kneeling on gravel.

105
00:09:20,031 --> 00:09:21,351
Is that a yes?

106
00:09:21,571 --> 00:09:24,851
Yes. Yes. Get up.

107
00:09:29,351 --> 00:09:31,042
Mom wants an engagement dinner.

108
00:09:31,092 --> 00:09:33,751
I said you'd host. Your place, your rules.

109
00:09:35,441 --> 00:09:36,621
My place?

110
00:09:37,901 --> 00:09:40,801
Well, look at that. He did good.

111
00:09:41,629 --> 00:09:43,049
He did okay.

112
00:09:43,739 --> 00:09:46,792
Your mother got a ring
out of a gumball machine.

113
00:09:46,842 --> 00:09:48,499
Wore it eleven years.

114
00:09:49,859 --> 00:09:51,759
The dinner's Saturday. Here.

115
00:09:52,789 --> 00:09:54,629
I'll get the grey suit cleaned.

116
00:09:56,079 --> 00:09:57,799
About that.

117
00:09:58,789 --> 00:10:00,469
Would you mind staying in the cottage?

118
00:10:00,519 --> 00:10:02,289
Just for the dinner. It's not about you.

119
00:10:02,339 --> 00:10:04,049
They're just, Celeste is a lot.

120
00:10:08,521 --> 00:10:11,061
I'll make sure the roses
look nice from the window.

121
00:10:12,619 --> 00:10:13,619
Dad.

122
00:10:14,339 --> 00:10:16,499
It's fine. I'll watch the game.

123
00:10:20,867 --> 00:10:23,278
Two servers. Two! On a Saturday.

124
00:10:23,328 --> 00:10:29,087
I have six courses and a lady in
green who already sent back the bread.

125
00:10:30,325 --> 00:10:31,785
Where are the aprons?

126
00:10:33,515 --> 00:10:34,635
Who are you?

127
00:10:35,235 --> 00:10:36,201
I live out back.

128
00:10:36,251 --> 00:10:40,615
I've carried trays at more weddings
than you've had hot dinners.

129
00:10:42,124 --> 00:10:43,484
You're an angel.

130
00:10:45,544 --> 00:10:47,044
Don't tell my daughter.

131
00:10:48,094 --> 00:10:50,274
Still no father tonight, Hannah?

132
00:10:50,879 --> 00:10:53,379
He's away. Portugal.

133
00:10:54,039 --> 00:10:56,699
Portugal. In November.

134
00:10:57,579 --> 00:10:58,579
Mom.

135
00:11:11,639 --> 00:11:13,699
And who's this? He's very good.

136
00:11:15,999 --> 00:11:18,759
Oh, he's just our old gardener.

137
00:11:20,469 --> 00:11:23,129
Well, he pours better than he dresses.

138
00:11:30,579 --> 00:11:32,079
Enjoy your dinner, ma'am.

139
00:11:54,657 --> 00:11:55,697
You okay?

140
00:11:56,597 --> 00:11:59,937
Never better. They liked the wine.

141
00:12:01,295 --> 00:12:03,875
I'm hiding. Don't tell anyone.

142
00:12:05,254 --> 00:12:07,334
Hiding's free back here.

143
00:12:09,284 --> 00:12:09,883
Those roses.

144
00:12:09,933 --> 00:12:15,804
My mother's been through three gardeners in five years,
and none of them could grow anything like that.

145
00:12:16,572 --> 00:12:20,832
Don't fuss them.
Most people fuss roses to death.

146
00:12:21,502 --> 00:12:23,902
That's it? That's the secret?

147
00:12:25,379 --> 00:12:27,609
That, and my wife planted that one.

148
00:12:27,659 --> 00:12:29,505
It'd be rude to die on her.

149
00:12:29,555 --> 00:12:30,555
Julian.

150
00:12:35,065 --> 00:12:37,725
Elijah. Nice to meet you, sir.

151
00:12:38,755 --> 00:12:42,555
Please don't call me sir.
My mother'll hear and think it's working.

152
00:12:53,075 --> 00:12:54,495
You're still up.

153
00:12:55,215 --> 00:12:59,495
Slugs come out at night.
Somebody has to tell them no.

154
00:13:00,375 --> 00:13:01,815
Dad, about tonight.

155
00:13:03,175 --> 00:13:06,535
The lamb was good. Delia can cook.

156
00:13:08,479 --> 00:13:09,479
Dad.

157
00:13:11,289 --> 00:13:15,657
I heard you. I've been
called worse by better.

158
00:13:15,707 --> 00:13:21,786
You don't know these people.
If she knew, she'd look at me different.

159
00:13:21,836 --> 00:13:22,847
Forever.

160
00:13:23,735 --> 00:13:31,835
Maybe. Go to bed. You've got a
wedding to plan, and I've got slugs.

161
00:13:37,864 --> 00:13:40,344
Your girl's getting married, Miriam.

162
00:13:42,436 --> 00:13:43,776
Who does these?

163
00:13:45,086 --> 00:13:46,466
Our gardener.

164
00:13:48,116 --> 00:13:49,796
Your wine man.

165
00:13:50,406 --> 00:13:52,946
You. What do you charge?

166
00:13:54,886 --> 00:13:56,626
Depends on the garden, ma'am.

167
00:13:59,266 --> 00:14:03,137
Mine's a disgrace, and there's
a wedding in it in nine weeks.

168
00:14:03,187 --> 00:14:04,966
Twenty an hour. Monday.

169
00:14:05,274 --> 00:14:06,374
Twenty-two.

170
00:14:12,464 --> 00:14:14,493
I'm worth the two dollars, ma'am.

171
00:14:14,543 --> 00:14:15,724
Ask the roses.

172
00:14:16,044 --> 00:14:19,544
Twenty-two. And you'll use the side gate.

173
00:14:20,393 --> 00:14:22,890
One more thing. The wedding arch.

174
00:14:22,940 --> 00:14:25,633
I'd want to grow it from these.

175
00:14:26,096 --> 00:14:28,056
Fine. Make it pretty.

176
00:14:31,414 --> 00:14:32,654
Dad, what are you doing?

177
00:14:33,244 --> 00:14:34,684
Gettin' a raise.

178
00:14:37,884 --> 00:14:39,124
I'm serious.

179
00:14:40,314 --> 00:14:44,293
So am I. You're getting
married under something I grew.

180
00:14:44,343 --> 00:14:46,494
Don't you take that from me.

181
00:14:46,544 --> 00:14:48,657
Side gate. Always the side gate.

182
00:14:48,707 --> 00:14:50,616
Boots off before the terrace.

183
00:14:50,666 --> 00:14:55,764
You don't speak to the family unless
they speak to you, and they won't.

184
00:14:57,524 --> 00:14:58,564
Yes, sir.

185
00:14:59,924 --> 00:15:02,417
And the roses on the east wall are dead.

186
00:15:02,467 --> 00:15:05,023
She'll tell you it was the last gardener.

187
00:15:05,073 --> 00:15:07,724
It was her. She waters them at night.

188
00:15:09,533 --> 00:15:11,413
Evenings. That'll do it.

189
00:15:11,853 --> 00:15:15,673
Walter. Not sir. I only dress like one.

190
00:15:45,871 --> 00:15:46,871
Boots.

191
00:15:48,296 --> 00:15:49,336
Ma'am?

192
00:15:50,293 --> 00:15:52,553
You're on my terrace in boots.

193
00:15:54,833 --> 00:15:56,709
Just cutting through to the shed, ma'am.

194
00:15:56,759 --> 00:15:57,759
I'll go round.

195
00:16:00,794 --> 00:16:02,474
Since you're here.

196
00:16:09,621 --> 00:16:11,921
Well, I can't use it now, can I?

197
00:16:18,741 --> 00:16:19,741
Afternoon, Miss Moore.

198
00:16:20,789 --> 00:16:22,009
Afternoon.

199
00:16:27,286 --> 00:16:29,346
You don't have to let her do that.

200
00:16:31,216 --> 00:16:32,676
Neither do you.

201
00:16:35,186 --> 00:16:36,486
That's not fair.

202
00:16:36,536 --> 00:16:39,016
No. It isn't.

203
00:16:45,102 --> 00:16:48,999
No, listen to me. Listen.
It's three point two, not three.

204
00:16:49,049 --> 00:16:52,878
Nobody's going to look past
her name, it's on every page.

205
00:16:52,928 --> 00:16:55,542
I made sure she signed in a hurry.

206
00:16:59,679 --> 00:17:02,259
Because she's a nobody, Danny. No family.

207
00:17:02,309 --> 00:17:04,248
A dad who's always in Portugal.

208
00:17:04,298 --> 00:17:06,459
Who's going to fight for her?

209
00:17:11,790 --> 00:17:14,234
And on Friday I'm making her partner.

210
00:17:14,284 --> 00:17:18,290
A partner's signature hangs
better than an associate's.

211
00:17:19,560 --> 00:17:24,910
The wedding? Celeste will cancel it
herself the minute anybody says fraud.

212
00:17:24,960 --> 00:17:26,500
I know my sister.

213
00:17:32,409 --> 00:17:33,429
Who's there?

214
00:17:33,999 --> 00:17:37,839
Just me, sir. Deadheading.

215
00:17:39,117 --> 00:17:40,877
How long have you been back there?

216
00:17:42,277 --> 00:17:44,512
Long enough to get the whites done.

217
00:17:44,562 --> 00:17:46,037
The reds are next.

218
00:17:47,347 --> 00:17:51,447
Good roses. Shame if you
got careless with those.

219
00:18:04,787 --> 00:18:06,027
Sit down a minute.

220
00:18:07,437 --> 00:18:10,217
Dad, it's eleven.
I've got a deposition at eight.

221
00:18:11,435 --> 00:18:13,775
Marcus was on the phone
in the garden today.

222
00:18:14,135 --> 00:18:15,135
Okay.

223
00:18:17,245 --> 00:18:19,232
He said three point two million.

224
00:18:19,282 --> 00:18:21,395
He said your name's on every page.

225
00:18:21,445 --> 00:18:25,245
He said you're a nobody and
nobody would fight for you.

226
00:18:26,069 --> 00:18:27,869
He would never say that.

227
00:18:29,679 --> 00:18:31,879
He said it to a man called Danny.

228
00:18:32,109 --> 00:18:35,342
Dad. Marcus has been
good to me for six years.

229
00:18:35,392 --> 00:18:40,189
My first winter, he bought me a
coat because I didn't have one.

230
00:18:42,277 --> 00:18:43,977
Did you read what you signed?

231
00:18:46,567 --> 00:18:48,887
You heard half a phone
call through a hedge.

232
00:18:50,347 --> 00:18:52,007
I heard what I heard.

233
00:18:54,637 --> 00:18:55,964
And what do I do with that?

234
00:18:56,014 --> 00:19:00,037
Walk into Richard Whitmore's office
and say the gardener heard something?

235
00:19:01,447 --> 00:19:03,307
I didn't mean—

236
00:19:05,317 --> 00:19:08,417
Yes, you did. It's all right. It's late.

237
00:19:15,737 --> 00:19:19,277
Because she's a nobody, Danny. No family.

238
00:19:28,507 --> 00:19:30,167
Get down from there.

239
00:19:32,175 --> 00:19:33,475
Two more ties.

240
00:19:35,005 --> 00:19:38,836
Get down before I have to explain
a dead gardener to Mrs. Whitmore.

241
00:19:38,886 --> 00:19:40,865
She'll want it off the books.

242
00:19:49,375 --> 00:19:51,915
Your ankles are the size of my head.

243
00:19:54,264 --> 00:19:55,444
It's the heat.

244
00:19:56,504 --> 00:19:59,664
It's not the heat. See a doctor.

245
00:20:00,742 --> 00:20:03,806
A hundred and eighty
dollars to be told to rest.

246
00:20:03,856 --> 00:20:06,622
I can rest for free when this is done.

247
00:20:17,312 --> 00:20:19,872
You look at her the way I
look at my granddaughter.

248
00:20:20,652 --> 00:20:22,292
None of my business.

249
00:20:23,522 --> 00:20:26,202
No. It isn't.

250
00:20:28,352 --> 00:20:29,952
Drink your water.

251
00:20:38,582 --> 00:20:40,522
Night, Dad.

252
00:20:41,802 --> 00:20:43,962
Night, baby girl. Eat something.

253
00:21:04,460 --> 00:21:05,980
Can I help you, sir?

254
00:21:09,278 --> 00:21:11,018
Looking for the gardener.

255
00:21:13,777 --> 00:21:15,377
In his coat, sir?

256
00:21:15,897 --> 00:21:17,577
Tell him I'd like a word.

257
00:21:30,607 --> 00:21:37,367
Sit. Good news first. The partnership vote
is Friday and I'm putting your name in.

258
00:21:38,087 --> 00:21:41,287
Marcus, are you serious?

259
00:21:41,625 --> 00:21:44,045
Youngest partner in the firm's history.

260
00:21:51,983 --> 00:21:53,123
How's Portugal?

261
00:21:57,642 --> 00:22:02,262
I'm not judging. Everybody's
embarrassed of something.

262
00:22:02,922 --> 00:22:05,342
My mother sold lipstick
out of a station wagon.

263
00:22:05,410 --> 00:22:06,710
What do you want?

264
00:22:09,028 --> 00:22:11,478
Your father's been
crouching in hedges on my

265
00:22:11,528 --> 00:22:14,248
sister's property,
listening to private calls.

266
00:22:14,788 --> 00:22:17,068
If Celeste finds out,
she calls the police.

267
00:22:17,933 --> 00:22:21,103
Then she asks why her
son's fiancée lied to her

268
00:22:21,153 --> 00:22:25,013
face at her own table,
and that's the wedding.

269
00:22:26,442 --> 00:22:28,302
He's not. He wouldn't.

270
00:22:29,630 --> 00:22:34,410
I want him off the estate.
And I don't want to see him at the wedding.

271
00:22:34,850 --> 00:22:38,030
Not serving, not standing
at the back. Nowhere.

272
00:22:39,590 --> 00:22:43,090
He's building the arch. It's his arch.

273
00:22:44,810 --> 00:22:47,090
Then it'll be a very nice arch.

274
00:22:49,568 --> 00:22:52,238
Friday, Hannah,
think about how far you've come,

275
00:22:52,288 --> 00:22:55,188
and whatever he thinks he heard,
make sure he forgets it.

276
00:22:58,028 --> 00:22:59,748
Dad, I need you to...

277
00:23:10,537 --> 00:23:11,917
You eat?

278
00:23:13,967 --> 00:23:14,967
Yeah.

279
00:23:21,527 --> 00:23:23,967
Dad, I need you to stop
going to the estate.

280
00:23:25,987 --> 00:23:27,887
The arch is two weeks from done.

281
00:23:28,067 --> 00:23:30,007
Somebody else can finish it.

282
00:23:33,685 --> 00:23:35,885
Nobody else knows those roses.

283
00:23:42,235 --> 00:23:43,875
Who told you to say this?

284
00:23:46,295 --> 00:23:48,015
Nobody told me anything.

285
00:23:50,283 --> 00:23:51,283
Marcus?

286
00:23:51,903 --> 00:23:55,633
It doesn't matter who.
If Celeste finds out you're

287
00:23:55,683 --> 00:23:58,923
my father after I lied
to her face, it's over.

288
00:24:00,583 --> 00:24:03,743
And she could have you arrested
for what you did in that garden.

289
00:24:04,063 --> 00:24:05,503
I'm trying to protect you.

290
00:24:08,603 --> 00:24:09,603
Okay.

291
00:24:11,523 --> 00:24:12,743
And the wedding?

292
00:24:17,043 --> 00:24:18,743
I don't think you should come.

293
00:24:27,282 --> 00:24:28,502
To the wedding?

294
00:24:28,862 --> 00:24:32,312
You'd be working it anyway.
She thinks you're staff.

295
00:24:32,362 --> 00:24:34,742
You'd be carrying trays
at your own daughter's.

296
00:24:37,570 --> 00:24:39,470
I'd have carried them.

297
00:24:41,320 --> 00:24:46,340
I know you would, I know.
That's why I can't let you.

298
00:24:52,053 --> 00:24:53,193
All right.

299
00:24:54,803 --> 00:24:55,803
Dad.

300
00:24:56,980 --> 00:25:00,880
I said, all right, go in. It's cold.

301
00:25:12,490 --> 00:25:14,270
Monday's my last day.

302
00:25:16,080 --> 00:25:18,060
The arch isn't finished.

303
00:25:20,708 --> 00:25:21,748
I know.

304
00:25:23,618 --> 00:25:25,258
Did she fire you?

305
00:25:26,848 --> 00:25:30,108
Nobody fired me. Family things.

306
00:25:30,908 --> 00:25:32,348
Family things.

307
00:25:37,928 --> 00:25:39,937
You keep touching that pocket.

308
00:25:39,987 --> 00:25:41,127
Something I heard.

309
00:25:42,247 --> 00:25:45,327
If I play it, everybody
finds out she lied about me.

310
00:25:46,347 --> 00:25:50,067
Then she loses the wedding anyway,
just from the other side.

311
00:25:50,813 --> 00:25:52,533
So you do nothing.

312
00:25:53,973 --> 00:25:55,973
I finish the arch.

313
00:25:59,407 --> 00:26:02,107
The East Gate isn't locked before six.

314
00:26:02,167 --> 00:26:04,867
I'm up at five. Nobody else is.

315
00:26:06,795 --> 00:26:08,615
Why would I need to know that?

316
00:26:09,545 --> 00:26:11,225
No reason at all.

317
00:26:40,065 --> 00:26:43,555
To the youngest partner in
the history of this firm.

318
00:27:04,813 --> 00:27:07,593
There you go, Miriam. All done.

319
00:27:25,793 --> 00:27:31,123
A man's collapsed. The Whitmore Estate,
the garden, come in by the East Gate.

320
00:27:31,173 --> 00:27:33,913
He's breathing,
but only just. Please hurry.

321
00:27:37,751 --> 00:27:41,991
Stay with me. Mornings,
not evenings, remember?

322
00:27:42,251 --> 00:27:43,871
Who's going to water the thing?

323
00:27:45,331 --> 00:27:50,521
Mr. Julian, it's Walter, it's the
gardener, he's going to St. Mary's.

324
00:27:50,571 --> 00:27:53,971
Sir, I think you'd better tell Miss Moore,
I think he's her father.

325
00:28:01,329 --> 00:28:05,169
Hannah. Walter found Elijah in the garden.

326
00:28:05,349 --> 00:28:06,789
He's on his way to St. Mary's.

327
00:28:10,868 --> 00:28:13,908
Hannah, is he your father?

328
00:28:16,036 --> 00:28:17,056
Yes.

329
00:28:17,644 --> 00:28:21,984
Pressure's 210 over 120.
Get a line in, call nephrology.

330
00:28:27,683 --> 00:28:29,003
Are you family?

331
00:28:30,403 --> 00:28:33,293
I'm his daughter, Elijah Moore.

332
00:28:33,343 --> 00:28:34,343
He's my father.

333
00:28:37,723 --> 00:28:40,023
Your father's kidney is failing.

334
00:28:40,343 --> 00:28:41,843
It's very advanced.

335
00:28:42,693 --> 00:28:44,943
Kidney? Kidneys?

336
00:28:45,183 --> 00:28:47,923
No. He only has one.

337
00:28:48,153 --> 00:28:52,213
That's not right. He's never had surgery.

338
00:28:52,413 --> 00:28:54,333
He's never been sick a day in his life.

339
00:28:54,461 --> 00:28:56,721
There's a scar on his left side.

340
00:28:57,001 --> 00:28:59,121
It's old. Seven or eight years.

341
00:29:00,401 --> 00:29:04,081
Somebody took a kidney out of your father
and they knew what they were doing.

342
00:29:08,759 --> 00:29:11,099
Eight years ago,
I was starting law school.

343
00:29:11,348 --> 00:29:14,648
The man who brought him in
said he's been working nights.

344
00:29:14,968 --> 00:29:17,908
In the cold. With his kidney like this,

345
00:29:18,068 --> 00:29:19,988
that's the last thing he
should have been doing.

346
00:29:20,958 --> 00:29:22,518
Working on what?

347
00:29:23,088 --> 00:29:24,888
He said an arch.

348
00:29:30,318 --> 00:29:33,278
Without a transplant, we're talking weeks.

349
00:29:33,978 --> 00:29:35,798
Dialysis will buy us some time.

350
00:29:36,438 --> 00:29:37,958
Is there any other family?

351
00:29:38,816 --> 00:29:40,436
It's just me.

352
00:29:45,716 --> 00:29:48,996
His things. The coat's wet, I'm sorry.

353
00:29:54,034 --> 00:29:57,494
Hannah, I'm so sorry to do this today.

354
00:29:58,574 --> 00:30:02,134
The auditors found 3.2 million
missing from the Whitmore Trust.

355
00:30:02,634 --> 00:30:04,114
Every transfer has your signature.

356
00:30:05,033 --> 00:30:07,313
Marcus, I signed what
you put in front of me.

357
00:30:07,811 --> 00:30:12,331
Then you should have read it.
You're suspended, effective now.

358
00:30:12,571 --> 00:30:13,571
Don't come in.

359
00:30:15,359 --> 00:30:17,519
I did what you asked. I sent him away.

360
00:30:17,748 --> 00:30:21,148
And I appreciate it.
Read before you sign, Hannah.

361
00:30:25,718 --> 00:30:27,378
He tried to tell me.

362
00:31:09,907 --> 00:31:17,227
Greenfield, you made it up.
You spelled pleased wrong.

363
00:31:24,815 --> 00:31:26,715
I called you the gardener.

364
00:31:31,025 --> 00:31:36,345
Fraud, Julian. Three million dollars,
it'll be in every paper by tomorrow.

365
00:31:37,563 --> 00:31:38,943
She didn't do it.

366
00:31:39,953 --> 00:31:42,073
Marcus says the signatures.

367
00:31:43,303 --> 00:31:44,743
Marcus says.

368
00:31:46,073 --> 00:31:50,033
The wedding is off.
I'm calling the planner tonight.

369
00:31:50,573 --> 00:31:53,873
Call whoever you like.
I'm still marrying her.

370
00:31:53,948 --> 00:31:58,168
With what? Your father will cut you off.

371
00:31:59,167 --> 00:32:01,247
Then I'll be poor and married.

372
00:32:12,965 --> 00:32:14,605
He's not the gardener.

373
00:32:15,223 --> 00:32:18,933
I know. I should have
seen it at the dinner.

374
00:32:18,983 --> 00:32:22,363
He filled your glass last.
Nobody does that for a stranger.

375
00:32:26,782 --> 00:32:32,322
He sold his kidney, Julian,
for law school, $40,000.

376
00:32:33,102 --> 00:32:35,002
He told me it was a scholarship.

377
00:32:35,720 --> 00:32:39,740
He made up a whole foundation
and he spelled pleased wrong.

378
00:32:40,360 --> 00:32:43,480
And Marcus showed me a picture
and offered me partner,

379
00:32:44,000 --> 00:32:47,560
and I went home and told my
father not to come to my wedding.

380
00:32:48,320 --> 00:32:49,580
And he said, all right.

381
00:32:50,478 --> 00:32:53,338
And then he went and finished
the arch in the dark,

382
00:32:53,678 --> 00:32:56,438
so it'd be ready for a wedding
he wasn't allowed to see.

383
00:32:57,388 --> 00:32:59,628
I traded my father for a title.

384
00:33:00,997 --> 00:33:02,817
Why?

385
00:33:05,557 --> 00:33:07,797
Because the first time it was easier.

386
00:33:08,517 --> 00:33:09,717
And then it was a habit.

387
00:33:11,585 --> 00:33:13,345
Do you still want to marry me?

388
00:33:15,033 --> 00:33:16,033
Yes.

389
00:33:16,943 --> 00:33:18,783
Then I want to meet your father.

390
00:33:19,543 --> 00:33:22,743
Properly. Not the wine man. Your dad.

391
00:33:23,192 --> 00:33:25,092
He's dying, Julian.

392
00:33:26,832 --> 00:33:28,472
Then we'd better hurry.

393
00:33:32,727 --> 00:33:35,267
If you're a match,
I'll be honest with you.

394
00:33:36,007 --> 00:33:37,527
It's not a small surgery.

395
00:33:39,045 --> 00:33:40,485
Neither was his.

396
00:33:49,569 --> 00:33:54,069
Mr. Moore, we have a match,
a very good one.

397
00:33:54,379 --> 00:33:55,719
Somebody died.

398
00:33:55,952 --> 00:33:58,692
No, a living donor.

399
00:34:02,172 --> 00:34:03,172
No.

400
00:34:04,982 --> 00:34:05,537
Dad.

401
00:34:05,587 --> 00:34:09,207
No, Doctor. She's getting married.

402
00:34:09,667 --> 00:34:10,667
Tell her no.

403
00:34:11,727 --> 00:34:13,407
I'll give you two a minute.

404
00:34:18,177 --> 00:34:19,757
I found the box.

405
00:34:21,277 --> 00:34:25,557
The Greenfield Foundation.
You spelt pleased wrong.

406
00:34:26,337 --> 00:34:27,937
Eight years, Dad.

407
00:34:29,557 --> 00:34:31,247
Every time I bought a
nice coat, every time

408
00:34:31,297 --> 00:34:33,417
I walked into court,
I thought, look at me.

409
00:34:33,546 --> 00:34:37,526
I did this. I did all of this by myself.

410
00:34:38,066 --> 00:34:39,686
And you let me think that.

411
00:34:40,894 --> 00:34:44,354
You did do it. I just paid the fee.

412
00:34:46,284 --> 00:34:50,884
You paid with your body. And I told
them you were a friend of the family.

413
00:34:51,044 --> 00:34:52,744
Then I told them you were the gardener.

414
00:34:53,242 --> 00:34:55,542
Then I told you not to come to my wedding.

415
00:34:56,002 --> 00:34:58,402
Three times. I count all three.

416
00:34:58,661 --> 00:34:59,961
I don't.

417
00:35:02,841 --> 00:35:03,941
I do.

418
00:35:08,561 --> 00:35:10,731
You always told me to hold my head up.

419
00:35:10,781 --> 00:35:15,661
I can't. Not if you die in here because
I was too ashamed to say your name.

420
00:35:16,229 --> 00:35:20,459
So I'm gonna say it to anybody
who'll listen and you're gonna

421
00:35:20,509 --> 00:35:23,397
take my kidney and you're
gonna walk me down that aisle.

422
00:35:23,447 --> 00:35:29,387
And you're not going to argue with me
because I'm a lawyer and I will win.

423
00:35:32,766 --> 00:35:34,386
You're your mother.

424
00:35:35,656 --> 00:35:37,016
Is that a yes?

425
00:35:39,676 --> 00:35:42,136
Your mother never let me say no either.

426
00:35:53,036 --> 00:35:54,116
You scared?

427
00:35:56,846 --> 00:35:58,226
Terrified.

428
00:35:58,886 --> 00:36:03,186
Me too. First time I did this,
I was by myself.

429
00:36:03,886 --> 00:36:04,986
This is better.

430
00:36:19,986 --> 00:36:23,526
Dad, what are you doing here?

431
00:36:24,424 --> 00:36:28,344
Walter told me about the gardener.

432
00:36:30,514 --> 00:36:32,454
Your mother doesn't know I'm here.

433
00:36:33,862 --> 00:36:35,242
Are you gonna tell her?

434
00:36:36,062 --> 00:36:40,242
Eventually, I'd like to see her face.

435
00:36:50,412 --> 00:36:54,112
It's working.
It started working on the table.

436
00:36:59,062 --> 00:37:02,342
His coat. Walter brought it.

437
00:37:07,671 --> 00:37:10,316
Because she's a nobody, Danny. No family.

438
00:37:10,366 --> 00:37:12,354
A dad who's always in Portugal.

439
00:37:12,404 --> 00:37:14,611
Who's going to fight for her?

440
00:37:17,794 --> 00:37:22,874
He recorded it. He recorded it and I
told him he heard half a phone call.

441
00:37:24,492 --> 00:37:25,772
That's my uncle.

442
00:37:27,232 --> 00:37:28,572
That's evidence.

443
00:37:33,952 --> 00:37:38,512
From the arch. I watered
it mornings, not evenings.

444
00:37:38,732 --> 00:37:40,052
You remembered.

445
00:37:43,017 --> 00:37:47,617
Walter, did anybody
ever ask you about this?

446
00:37:52,077 --> 00:37:54,187
Mr. Hale went through
his coat in the potting

447
00:37:54,237 --> 00:37:56,757
shed, the week before he stopped coming.

448
00:37:56,846 --> 00:38:01,166
Every pocket. I asked if I could help him.

449
00:38:01,426 --> 00:38:02,546
He didn't like that.

450
00:38:03,994 --> 00:38:05,634
He was looking for this.

451
00:38:07,154 --> 00:38:10,714
Then I'll say so,
to whoever needs to hear it.

452
00:38:15,543 --> 00:38:19,123
I'll keep this short because it's painful.

453
00:38:20,463 --> 00:38:23,723
Every transfer, every single
one was signed by Hannah Moore.

454
00:38:24,541 --> 00:38:26,561
I brought her into this family.

455
00:38:27,081 --> 00:38:28,781
I take responsibility for that.

456
00:38:29,801 --> 00:38:31,451
You couldn't have known, Marcus.

457
00:38:31,501 --> 00:38:32,501
I should have.

458
00:38:34,861 --> 00:38:37,621
Richard, I'd recommend we hand this
to the district attorney today.

459
00:38:37,760 --> 00:38:40,500
No rush. We have time.

460
00:38:46,758 --> 00:38:49,698
Hannah, you shouldn't be here.

461
00:38:49,878 --> 00:38:52,018
I'm still a member of the bar.
Sit down, Marcus.

462
00:38:54,228 --> 00:38:55,368
This one's short, too.

463
00:39:06,926 --> 00:39:09,146
That's a cheap phone and a hedge.

464
00:39:09,486 --> 00:39:10,566
That could be anybody.

465
00:39:11,736 --> 00:39:15,556
It's you, talking to Danny
Coyle at First Harbor Bank.

466
00:39:16,766 --> 00:39:19,526
We traced the money this
morning, Mr. Chairman.

467
00:39:19,886 --> 00:39:22,566
The account it went to
is in Mr. Hale's name.

468
00:39:24,056 --> 00:39:25,076
Marcus.

469
00:39:26,546 --> 00:39:27,946
Celeste.

470
00:39:28,646 --> 00:39:29,646
Walter?

471
00:39:32,115 --> 00:39:36,475
Mr. Hale searched the gardener's coat
in the potting shed, sir, every pocket.

472
00:39:36,675 --> 00:39:38,075
He was looking for that phone.

473
00:39:39,183 --> 00:39:41,323
You're taking the word of a butler?

474
00:39:41,503 --> 00:39:45,183
For 31 years. Sit down, Marcus.

475
00:39:45,561 --> 00:39:50,181
The gardener. Why would the gardener
be in the hedge with a phone?

476
00:39:50,501 --> 00:39:54,001
Because he's my father, Elijah Moore.

477
00:39:56,960 --> 00:40:00,820
Marcus found out. He made me partner.

478
00:40:01,480 --> 00:40:03,980
And the price was that my father
didn't come to my wedding.

479
00:40:05,420 --> 00:40:10,900
I said yes. He finished your son's
arch at four in the morning by himself.

480
00:40:11,070 --> 00:40:13,190
And then he collapsed under it.

481
00:40:14,990 --> 00:40:17,190
That's the man you made
pick up your napkin.

482
00:40:21,698 --> 00:40:23,278
I made you partner.

483
00:40:24,258 --> 00:40:25,538
I resign.

484
00:40:29,658 --> 00:40:30,958
Marcus Hale.

485
00:40:32,888 --> 00:40:34,828
I gave you everything.

486
00:40:36,136 --> 00:40:39,636
You gave me a coat. He gave me a kidney.

487
00:40:44,406 --> 00:40:48,906
All in favor of clearing Miss Moore
and removing Mr. Hale as trustee.

488
00:40:55,086 --> 00:41:01,006
One more. I move that Celeste Whitmore
be removed from the trust board.

489
00:41:03,025 --> 00:41:04,025
Richard.

490
00:41:04,715 --> 00:41:07,255
You defended him for an hour, Celeste.

491
00:41:07,935 --> 00:41:09,995
You never once asked the gardener's name.

492
00:41:21,773 --> 00:41:24,173
Why didn't he just tell me who he was?

493
00:41:25,793 --> 00:41:29,093
Because I asked him not to.
That part's on me.

494
00:41:31,733 --> 00:41:34,633
I would never have spoken to
him like that if I'd known.

495
00:41:36,293 --> 00:41:38,873
I know. That's the problem.

496
00:41:53,997 --> 00:41:56,247
Your mother would have cried
through the whole thing.

497
00:41:56,297 --> 00:41:59,137
You're crying.

498
00:41:59,297 --> 00:42:01,657
Pollen.

499
00:42:19,835 --> 00:42:21,055
Thank you, sir.

500
00:42:21,975 --> 00:42:25,335
Elijah, or Dad if you're brave.

501
00:42:26,235 --> 00:42:27,935
You may kiss the bride.

502
00:42:42,685 --> 00:42:44,445
Mr. Moore, you don't have to.

503
00:42:45,035 --> 00:42:48,235
Not tonight, Dad. Tonight you sit.

504
00:42:51,214 --> 00:42:57,334
Hi. Sorry. I'll be quick. My husband
says I talk like I'm billing by the hour.

505
00:43:00,312 --> 00:43:03,902
A few months ago at our engagement
dinner, somebody asked me who

506
00:43:03,952 --> 00:43:08,232
the man pouring the wine was,
and I said he's just our old gardener.

507
00:43:09,040 --> 00:43:11,880
I said it because I was scared
of what you'd think of me.

508
00:43:13,440 --> 00:43:15,080
That's the truth,
so here's the rest of it.

509
00:43:15,130 --> 00:43:19,030
This is my father, Elijah Moore.

510
00:43:19,890 --> 00:43:22,080
He grew every rose in this garden.

511
00:43:22,130 --> 00:43:25,930
He put me through law school with a
part of himself he never got back,

512
00:43:26,790 --> 00:43:31,250
and he never asked me for anything,
not even to say his name.

513
00:43:31,370 --> 00:43:35,070
Dad, everything I am is yours.

514
00:43:41,299 --> 00:43:46,139
